I"8<p>A conversational model hides several engineering problems behind a simple interface. It needs to learn language, respond to instructions, and turn its predictions into something a person can use. A voice assistant adds another challenge: it must begin speaking soon enough for the exchange to feel natural.</p>

<p><a href="https://github.com/jingyaogong/minimind">MiniMind</a> and <a href="https://github.com/gpt-omni/mini-omni">Mini-Omni</a> expose different parts of this process. MiniMind provides a small language model and its training pipeline. Mini-Omni builds speech interaction around a pretrained text model, coordinating the generation of words and audio.</p>

<p>Their common value is making consequential design choices small enough to inspect. They are independent projects with different starting points, architectures, and goals.</p>

